+# CMR-1 INTEGRATED JOURNEY (docs/product/cmr1-native-staging.md; founder acceptance cmr1-acceptance.md)
+#
+# One fresh account, the whole loop the founder named, typed, on a simulator against the RC's own
+# Supabase preview branch (migration + the RC gateway with the model key):
+#
+#   onboarding, four people added by name → a natural story in the K36 shape, told from the child's
+#   page ("Grace has not been sleeping very well and has been very clingy to my wife Rosa.") → the
+#   review ("Here's what I'll remember.") with no one called "Has" → a genuinely ambiguous person
+#   (two Mateos: "Which Mateo do you mean?", answered once) → the line on that Mateo's page only →
+#   Undo of that whole Tell → a note naming nobody, found under "Your words" (People's foot,
+#   notebook_deck) and its Source ("Your note") → a line's source from Grace's page ("You told
+#   Kinship · … · open the note") → correcting a line's words ("Edit words" → Save) → declining a
+#   reading ("Not this" → "Forget it") while the Tell's words stay on Grace's Pages → a promise due
+#   today becomes Today's Moment ("You said you'd call Rosa tonight.") → Message hand-off (the
+#   simulator opens Messages; nothing is sent) → return to Kinship → the return check when it is due.
+#
+# VOICE IS NOT DRIVEN HERE. A simulator has no microphone and SFSpeechRecognizer is unavailable, so
+# K34 (a spoken passage kept once) and the spoken scenarios (cmr1-acceptance.md 2 and 5) stay with the
+# founder's device pass. Everything below is typed.
+#
+# Names are placeholders from the CMR-1 eval rosters (evals/cmr1/rosters.json: "hart" and "circle"),
+# invented people only. Never the founder's family or People.
+#
+# Needs: a build of the e2e-staging profile (eas.json) pointed at the RC's preview branch; a dedicated,
+# NEVER-USED account on that branch with shell_v2, tell, ai_extraction, memory_v2 and notebook_deck on
+# through user_flag_overrides (e2e/make-staging-account.mjs --notebook); the branch's ai-gateway with
+# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set as that branch's own edge-function secret. The understanding is the live model,
+# so each wait is generous and the few places a model may honestly ask are handled either way.
+# The hand-off needs a contact with a phone number: a fresh simulator's own sample contacts (Kate Bell)
+# serve, through the system picker; nothing about them is stored.
+#
+#   maestro test .maestro/cmr1-journey.yaml \
+#     -e E2E_JOURNEY_EMAIL=<a never-used staging account> -e E2E_JOURNEY_PASSWORD=<…>
+appId: com.zenroost.kinship
+env:
+  STORY: "Grace has not been sleeping very well and has been very clingy to my wife Rosa."
+  AMBIGUOUS: "Mateo loved the book I lent him."
+  NOBODY: "Ran into an old teammate from the city office. She is moving to Lisbon in March."
+  PROMISE: "I told Rosa I'd call her tonight."
+---
+- launchApp:
+    clearState: true
+    clearKeychain: true
+    permissions:
+      contacts: allow
+
+# ── Onboarding: promise → sign in (email, the one path automation can drive) → name → consent ──
+- assertVisible: "Remember what matters about the people you care about."
+- tapOn: "Use email"
+- tapOn: "Email"
+- inputText: ${E2E_JOURNEY_EMAIL}
+- tapOn: "Password"
+- inputText: ${E2E_JOURNEY_PASSWORD}
+- tapOn: "Sign in"
+- extendedWaitUntil:
+    visible: "What should Kinship call you?"
+    timeout: 20000
+- inputText: "Dana"
+- tapOn: "Continue"
+- assertVisible: "So Kinship can understand what you tell it"
+- tapOn: "Allow understanding"
+
+# ── Adding people: four by name (no contact is read; nobody is pre-selected) ──
+- assertVisible: "Who do you want to show up for?"
+- tapOn: "Add someone by name"
+- assertVisible: "Add someone"
+- tapOn: "Their name"
+- inputText: "Grace"
+- tapOn: "Done"
+- tapOn: "Add someone by name"
+- tapOn: "Their name"
+- inputText: "Rosa"
+- tapOn: "Done"
+- tapOn: "Add someone by name"
+- tapOn: "Their name"
+- inputText: "Mateo Vargas"
+- tapOn: "Done"
+- tapOn: "Add someone by name"
+- tapOn: "Their name"
+- inputText: "Mateo Lindgren"
+- tapOn: "Done"
+- assertVisible: "Continue with 4 people"
+- tapOn: "Continue with 4 people"
+
+# No birthdays were read, so setup asks for one thing to tell; the stories below are told from the
+# pages they belong to, as the founder's session does. Skipping is an approved exit (SETUP_COPY.skip).
+- assertVisible: "Tell Kinship one thing about someone."
+- tapOn: "Skip for now"
+- extendedWaitUntil:
+    visible: "Today"
+    timeout: 20000
+
+# ── K36 as a class: the story from the child's page; nobody called "Has"; two lines naming Grace ──
+- tapOn: "People"
+- assertVisible: "Grace"
+- assertVisible: "Mateo Vargas"
+- assertVisible: "Mateo Lindgren"
+- tapOn: "Grace"
+- assertVisible: "Tell Kinship about Grace"
+- tapOn: "Tell Kinship about Grace"
+- assertVisible: "About Grace. In your own words."
+- inputText: ${STORY}
+- tapOn: "Keep"
+- extendedWaitUntil:
+    visible: "(Here’s what I’ll remember\\.|Kept .*|One thing to check.*)"
+    timeout: 60000
+# "has not been sleeping" may be read as health: a held line is memory only after the user's yes.
+- runFlow:
+    when:
+      visible: "Needs your yes"
+    commands:
+      - repeat:
+          while:
+            visible: "Keep it"
+          commands:
+            - tapOn: "Keep it"
+- assertNotVisible: "Who is Has\\?"
+- assertNotVisible: "Which Has do you mean\\?"
+- assertNotVisible: "Add Has"
+- assertNotVisible: "Has isn't in your people yet\\."
+- assertVisible: "Grace .*(sleeping|clingy).*"
+- runFlow:
+    when:
+      visible: "Done"
+    commands:
+      - tapOn: "Done"
+# Grace's page: the lines are hers, in her name.
+- assertVisible: "Grace .*(sleeping|clingy).*"
+- assertNotVisible: "Has .*"
+- tapOn: "Back"
+
+# ── Genuine ambiguity: two Mateos → exactly one question, both offered; the answer places the line ──
+- tapOn: "Tell Kinship something.*"
+- assertVisible: "About anyone. In your own words."
+- inputText: ${AMBIGUOUS}
+- tapOn: "Keep"
+- extendedWaitUntil:
+    visible: "Which Mateo do you mean\\?"
+    timeout: 60000
+- assertVisible: "Mateo Vargas"
+- assertVisible: "Mateo Lindgren"
+- tapOn: "Mateo Vargas"
+- extendedWaitUntil:
+    visible: "Done"
+    timeout: 30000
+- tapOn: "Done"
+- extendedWaitUntil:
+    visible: "Kept for Mateo Vargas\\."
+    timeout: 30000
+- tapOn: "Mateo Vargas"
+- assertVisible: ".*loved the book.*"
+- tapOn: "Back"
+- tapOn: "Mateo Lindgren"
+- assertNotVisible: ".*loved the book.*"
+- tapOn: "Back"
+
+# ── Undo: the whole Tell and its line, gone, from the Kept card ──
+- assertVisible: "Kept for Mateo Vargas\\."
+- tapOn: "Undo"
+- assertNotVisible: "Kept for Mateo Vargas\\."
+- tapOn: "Mateo Vargas"
+- assertNotVisible: ".*loved the book.*"
+- tapOn: "Back"
+
+# ── Every retained Tell is findable: a note naming nobody → "Your words" at the foot of People → Source ──
+- tapOn: "Tell Kinship something.*"
+- inputText: ${NOBODY}
+- tapOn: "Keep"
+- extendedWaitUntil:
+    visible: "(Kept your words.*|Nothing added from that one.*|Who is this about\\?|Here’s what I’ll remember\\.)"
+    timeout: 60000
+# Should the model ask who this is about, nothing is guessed: the words are kept, nothing added.
+- runFlow:
+    when:
+      visible: "Who is this about\\?"
+    commands:
+      - tapOn: "Don’t keep"
+- runFlow:
+    when:
+      visible: "Done"
+    commands:
+      - tapOn: "Done"
+- extendedWaitUntil:
+    visible: "(Kept your words.*|Nothing added from that one.*)"
+    timeout: 30000
+- scrollUntilVisible:
+    element:
+      text: "Your words"
+    direction: DOWN
+- tapOn: "Your words"
+- assertVisible: "What you told Kinship that isn't about anyone in People yet.*"
+- assertVisible: "Ran into an old teammate.*"
+- tapOn: "Ran into an old teammate.*"
+- assertVisible: "Your note"
+- assertVisible: "Typed.*"
+- assertVisible: "Ran into an old teammate.*"
+- tapOn: "Back"
+- tapOn: "Back"
+
+# ── A line's source, from Grace's page: the line sheet → "open the note" → the note ──
+- tapOn: "Grace"
+- tapOn: "Grace .*sleeping.*"
+- assertVisible: "You told Kinship.*open the note"
+- tapOn: "You told Kinship.*open the note"
+- assertVisible: "Your note"
+- assertVisible: "What Kinship kept from this"
+- assertVisible: "Grace has not been sleeping very well.*"
+- tapOn: "Back"
+
+# ── Correcting a reading: the user's words replace Kinship's; the edit wins ──
+- tapOn: "Grace .*sleeping.*"
+- tapOn: "Edit words"
+- assertVisible: "In your words"
+- tapOn: "What to remember"
+- eraseText: 300
+- inputText: "Grace has been sleeping badly lately"
+- tapOn: "Save"
+- assertVisible: "Grace has been sleeping badly lately.*"
+
+# ── Declining a reading: the line goes; the Tell's words stay on Grace's Pages ──
+- tapOn: "Grace .*clingy.*"
+- tapOn: "Not this"
+- assertVisible: "Forget this line\\? Your note stays exactly as you wrote it\\."
+- tapOn: "Forget it"
+- assertNotVisible: "Grace .*clingy.*"
+- tapOn: "Pages"
+- assertVisible: ".*You told Kinship"
+- assertVisible: "Grace has not been sleeping very well and has been very clingy to my wife Rosa\\."
+- tapOn: "Back"
+
+# ── A Today Moment from a trusted memory: the user's own promise, due today ──
+- tapOn: "Rosa"
+- tapOn: "Tell Kinship about Rosa"
+- inputText: ${PROMISE}
+- tapOn: "Keep"
+- extendedWaitUntil:
+    visible: "(Here’s what I’ll remember\\.|Kept .*|One thing to check.*)"
+    timeout: 60000
+- runFlow:
+    when:
+      visible: "Needs your yes"
+    commands:
+      - repeat:
+          while:
+            visible: "Keep it"
+          commands:
+            - tapOn: "Keep it"
+- runFlow:
+    when:
+      visible: "Done"
+    commands:
+      - tapOn: "Done"
+- tapOn: "Back"
+- tapOn: "Today"
+- extendedWaitUntil:
+    visible: "You said you.d .*Rosa.*"
+    timeout: 30000
+- assertVisible: "I did this"
+
+# ── Hand-off: Message opens Messages; nothing is sent; Kinship never stores the number ──
+- tapOn: "Message Rosa"
+# Rosa was typed, not picked from Contacts, so the sheet asks which contact she is (read at tap time).
+- runFlow:
+    when:
+      visible: "Choose Rosa"
+    commands:
+      - tapOn: "Choose Rosa"
+      - tapOn: "Kate Bell"
+- extendedWaitUntil:
+    visible: "Open Messages"
+    timeout: 15000
+- tapOn: "Open Messages"
+- launchApp:
+    stopApp: false
+
+# ── Return check: the app returns to Kinship, never a 1.0 screen; the question when it is due ──
+- assertVisible: "Today"
+- runFlow:
+    when:
+      visible: "Did you .*Rosa.*\\?"
+    commands:
+      - tapOn: "Yes"
+- assertVisible: "Today"
