+# CMR-1 native staging: the simulator run on EAS, against the RC's own Supabase branch
+
+**Status: PREPARED, NOT RUN. Nothing below happens without the founder's yes at each marked step; nothing here
+touches production.** Companion to `cmr1-release-plan.md` (the NATIVE-SIMULATOR row reads NOT RUN) and
+`cmr1-acceptance.md`. This is the only native path open to a cloud session: Linux, no KVM, no Mac, no Remote
+Control to a Mac, so the simulator has to be EAS-hosted. The files on `claude/cmr1-native-staging` (= the RC
+`fc974b7` + these):
+
+| File | What it is |
+|---|---|
+| `.eas/workflows/cmr1-native.yml` | Manual-dispatch EAS Workflow: build the iOS simulator app with `e2e-staging`, then run three Maestro flows on an EAS simulator |
+| `eas.json` → `e2e-staging` | A copy of `e2e-sim` without a Supabase target and without the local-networking entitlement (`EXPO_PUBLIC_E2E_LOCAL`); the branch URL and anon key arrive as workflow inputs, never committed. Every existing profile is byte-for-byte unchanged |
+| `.maestro/cmr1-journey.yaml` | The integrated typed journey the founder named (below). Voice is not driven: a simulator has no microphone and SFSpeechRecognizer is unavailable |
+| `e2e/make-staging-account.mjs` | Makes a never-used test account on a preview branch with the dogfood flags on for that account alone; refuses the production ref |
+
+## 1. How the staging works
+
+**The server.** The Supabase GitHub integration makes one preview branch per PR (`FUNCTIONS_DEPLOYED` when done).
+For PR #93 (`claude/cmr1-rc`) that branch would carry the RC's migration `20261114090000_v2_capture_understanding`
+(applied by the integration's *migrate* step) and be an isolated project: its own database, auth, API URL
+`https://<branch-ref>.supabase.co`, anon key and service-role key, no production data, no production accounts.
+
+Two things the integration does **not** give, verified on 15 Nov against the two preview branches that exist
+(`yycpamsjsroidfkfzcjn` for #90, `ourilvivxrmlwsroesbw` for #91) by listing their edge functions:
+
+1. **The branch does not run the PR's gateway.** Both branches' function records are identical to production's
+   (same function ids, `ai-gateway` **v17**, same bundle hash, same entrypoint path from the founder's Mac).
+   `FUNCTIONS_DEPLOYED` reports the integration's *deploy* step; the records say the step changed nothing. The
+   same was seen on PR #58 (`option-a-release-sequence.md`). So the RC gateway (v18) must be put on the branch by
+   hand, from the RC checkout, with the branch's ref, never production's:
+   `npx supabase functions deploy ai-gateway --project-ref <branch-ref> --use-api`. Then
+   `npx supabase functions download ai-gateway --project-ref <branch-ref> --use-api` and a diff against the
+   checkout, as the release plan does for production. This is a deploy to a throwaway project, but it is a deploy:
+   founder's yes (§4 b).
+2. **Secrets are branch-specific** (Supabase, "Managing secrets for branches": "Secrets set for one branch are not
+   automatically available in other branches"). The gateway reads the model key from the edge-function secret
+   **`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`** (`supabase/functions/ai-gateway/index.ts`). Without it every Tell on the branch fails
+   honestly ("Couldn't understand this one. Your words are kept…"), and the journey cannot pass. Only the founder
+   holds the key. The exact setting, either way:
+   - Dashboard: switch to the branch in the branch dropdown → **Edge Functions › Secrets** → add `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`
+     (this is the per-project secrets page, `https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/<branch-ref>/functions/secrets`).
+   - CLI: `npx supabase secrets set --project-ref <branch-ref> ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<the CMR-1 key>` (the value typed
+     into the shell by the founder, never into a chat or a file in the repo).
+   Use the dedicated CMR-1 key the founder already made (`cmr1-handoff.md` §2), and revoke it when the milestone
+   closes. `AI_DAILY_LIMIT`, `AI_CONSENT_VERSION`, `AI_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` keep their defaults (50, 1, none).
+
+**The accounts.** Two never-used accounts on the branch, made with the branch's service-role key (from the dashboard
+with the branch selected, Settings › API, or `npx supabase --experimental branches get claude/cmr1-rc -o env`):
+
+```bash
+# account A: the fresh-install gate, then smoke-tell (the alpha look the gate was written for: no notebook_deck)
+STAGING_API_URL=https://<branch-ref>.supabase.co STAGING_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<branch key> node e2e/make-staging-account.mjs
+# account B: the CMR-1 journey (the notebook look the founder's account has)
+STAGING_API_URL=https://<branch-ref>.supabase.co STAGING_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<branch key> node e2e/make-staging-account.mjs --notebook
+```
+
+Each writes `user_flag_overrides` rows for that user id only: `shell_v2`, `memory_v2`, `tell`, `ai_extraction`,
+`relationship_page_v2`, plus `notebook_deck` with `--notebook` and `voice_capture` with `--voice` (voice is on the
+founder's account, but a simulator cannot use it, so the journey account does without). `feature_flags` stays as the
+migrations leave it: every flag default off, rollout 0, so nobody else on the branch is on. These are the same rows
+the founder sets by hand for a real account; here they are on a project that will be deleted with the PR. The
+script refuses `kddpxiiyxgvjrtpdkvio` and any key minted for it. Credentials land in the gitignored
+`e2e/.captured/staging-account.<branch-ref>.local.json`.
+
+**The app.** EAS builds the `e2e-staging` profile for the simulator with `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and
+`EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` taken from the dispatch inputs (the workflow's build job `env`), so the branch's
+address is never in git. `EXPO_PUBLIC_V2_ENTRY=1` and analytics off, as `e2e-sim`. The anon key is a client key by
+design, but it still belongs to a throwaway project, which is why inputs rather than `eas.json`.
+
+**The flows**, in the order the workflow runs them on one EAS simulator (each starts with `clearState`; the server
+accounts persist between flows):
+
+1. `.maestro/cmr1-journey.yaml` on account B. Onboarding (email sign-in, name, consent) → four people added by name
+   (Grace, Rosa, Mateo Vargas, Mateo Lindgren: invented names from `evals/cmr1/rosters.json`, never the founder's
+   family) → the first-Tell step skipped (no birthdays were read) → from Grace's page, the K36-shaped story "Grace
+   has not been sleeping very well and has been very clingy to my wife Rosa." → the review: nobody called "Has", two
+   lines naming Grace, held lines kept on the user's yes → from the Tell pill, "Mateo loved the book I lent him." →
+   exactly "Which Mateo do you mean?", both offered, Vargas chosen → the line on Vargas's page, not Lindgren's →
+   Undo from the Kept card, the line gone → "Ran into an old teammate from the city office. She is moving to Lisbon
+   in March." → "Kept your words, under “Your words” in People" (or, if the model asks who, nothing is guessed:
+   Don't keep) → People's foot → Your words → the note → its Source ("Your note", "Typed") → Grace's page → a line →
+   "You told Kinship · … · open the note" → the Source with "What Kinship kept from this" → Edit words → Save →
+   Not this → Forget it: the line gone, the Tell's words still on Grace's Pages under "You told Kinship" → from
+   Rosa's page, "I told Rosa I'd call her tonight." → Today's Moment "You said you'd call Rosa tonight." with "I did
+   this" and "Message Rosa" → the hand-off (Rosa was typed, so "Which contact is Rosa?" → the system picker → the
+   simulator's own sample contact Kate Bell; nothing stored) → "Open Messages" → Messages opens → back to Kinship
+   on Today, never a 1.0 screen → "Did you call Rosa tonight?" answered Yes when it is shown (its timing is Jest's;
+   the flow does not wait ten minutes).
+2. `.maestro/fresh-install.yaml` on account A: the permanent gate, unchanged. **It needs a simulator contact "Maya
+   Okafor" with a birthday within 14 days and a mobile number** (its header). An EAS simulator has only the
+   sample contacts, so on EAS this flow fails at "Maya Okafor" unless that contact is seeded; the pre-packaged
+   Maestro job has no seeding step. Run it on EAS for the record (it proves promise → sign-in → setup is drawn), and
+   count it as a PASS only from a Mac (`xcrun simctl addmedia booted maya.vcf`), or ask for a custom job later.
+3. `.maestro/smoke-tell.yaml` on account A with `E2E_PERSON=Maya Okafor`: passes only after 2 did.
+
+A flow's failure does not undo the others' evidence: each uploads its own log and video to the run.
+
+**What this run proves, and does not.** NATIVE-SIMULATOR for the typed CMR-1 journey on the RC's own server
+code, with the live model: K36 as a class, genuine ambiguity asked once, every retained Tell findable, source,
+correction, decline, Undo, a grounded Moment, the hand-off and the return. It does not touch K34 (voice), the second
+phone, or anything on the founder's own data. FOUNDER-DEVICE stays the only tier that makes an item VERIFIED.
+
+## 2. Dispatching the workflow
+
+From a checkout of `claude/cmr1-native-staging` (or the RC once these files are on it), with the founder's EAS
+token in the shell (the cloud environment has it proxy-injected for `api.expo.dev`; `EXPO_TOKEN=proxy-injected`):
+
+```bash
+npx eas-cli workflow:validate .eas/workflows/cmr1-native.yml --non-interactive
+
+npx eas-cli workflow:run .eas/workflows/cmr1-native.yml --non-interactive \
+  -F supabase_url=https://<branch-ref>.supabase.co \
+  -F supabase_anon_key=<the branch's anon key> \
+  -F e2e_email=<account A email> -F e2e_password=<account A password> \
+  -F journey_email=<account B email> -F journey_password=<account B password>
+
+npx eas-cli workflow:runs                      # the run id
+npx eas-cli workflow:view <run id>             # jobs and their status
+npx eas-cli workflow:logs <run id>             # pick the Maestro job for the flow logs
+npx eas-cli workflow:insights:maestro          # per-flow pass/flake history, once there is some
+```
+
+`workflow:run` packages the working directory and uploads it (or `--ref <commit>` to build from git), so run it from a
+clean checkout. Inputs are stored with the run on expo.dev, visible to the account: the passwords are those of two
+throwaway staging accounts, the URL and key those of a project deleted with the PR. The Maestro job's `env` is how the
+flows receive `E2E_EMAIL`, `E2E_PASSWORD`, `E2E_PERSON`, `E2E_JOURNEY_EMAIL`, `E2E_JOURNEY_PASSWORD` (Maestro reads
+`${VAR}` from its environment when no `-e` is given).
+
+## 3. Expected cost
+
+Read on 15 Nov with read-only `eas-cli`/API calls:
+
+- **Plan: Free** (`thoroxnard`, subscription "Free", price 0). **`workflow:validate` of this file is refused on the
+  Free plan with "Running maestro_test jobs requires a paid plan"**, so the Maestro job cannot run at all until the
+  account is on a paid plan (expo.dev › Account settings › Billing). Everything else in the file validates (the
+  inputs and the build job were validated on their own: "Workflow configuration YAML is valid.").
+- **Build minutes.** The last `dogfood-v2` iOS device build (`dc8d97a2`, 11 Nov) took 341 s of build time on a
+  medium worker (queue 20 s, wait 3 s). A simulator Release build is of the same order: budget **6–8 build minutes**
+  per run, plus the queue. On a paid plan an iOS build is billed at that plan's per-minute rate once the plan's
+  included builds are used; on the Free plan it counts against the monthly free iOS build quota and runs at low
+  priority.
+- **Maestro minutes.** The three flows drive one simulator: the CMR-1 journey makes five live-model Tells with up to
+  60 s waits each; expect **8–12 minutes** of E2E time for the run (plus simulator boot and app install), billed at
+  the plan's E2E/Maestro per-minute rate. The exact rates were not readable from here (`docs.expo.dev` and the
+  billing page are outside this session's network); the founder reads them at Billing before approving.
+- **Model spend.** Five Tells on the branch gateway with the CMR-1 key, each one `relationship_extract` call plus a
+  possible re-read: a few cents. `AI_DAILY_LIMIT` (50 per user per day) caps it.
+- **Supabase.** A preview branch is billed per hour while active (it pauses when idle) at the organization's
+  branching rate; the integration deletes it when PR #93 closes or merges.
+
+No workflow has ever run on this account (`workflow:runs` is empty), so this is the first.
+
